[{:db/id 17592186308728 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" :question/id #uuid "d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37456" :question/problem "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(1,1)>0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$" :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det({f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=({f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-236e449f-8bdf-5cb7-898e-9834bb6e7cf6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-236e449f-8bdf-5cb7-898e-9834bb6e7cf6" :answer-field/id #uuid "236e449f-8bdf-5cb7-898e-9834bb6e7cf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7c4787e2-6983-5165-b71f-60ddbc84d9c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ac9e6ca-aa28-5456-80e0-6b2c6eed18c7" "answer-89c37704-a55e-55ef-8110-12970ee2c9ad" "answer-007def61-c0db-5afc-857c-bb1794f44c1f" "answer-7c4787e2-6983-5165-b71f-60ddbc84d9c2" "answer-e9eece08-2814-52b9-9cbf-85f258fc3528"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ac9e6ca-aa28-5456-80e0-6b2c6eed18c7" :answer/id #uuid "6ac9e6ca-aa28-5456-80e0-6b2c6eed18c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89c37704-a55e-55ef-8110-12970ee2c9ad" :answer/id #uuid "89c37704-a55e-55ef-8110-12970ee2c9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-007def61-c0db-5afc-857c-bb1794f44c1f" :answer/id #uuid "007def61-c0db-5afc-857c-bb1794f44c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III on